  Product key:  CU-FONTPRE-040
  Release:      April 24, 2026 (v1.3)

  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  Purpose:
    Emits <link rel="preload" as="font"> hints for LCP-critical fonts
    that Shopify's native font pipeline does not preload. Targets
    Shoplift-hosted commercial fonts (shop-assets/static_uploads/shoplift)
    which would otherwise only be discovered after CSS parse completes,
    adding 300-600ms to mobile LCP.

  Mechanism:
    Resource hint shifts the font fetch into the initial-priority batch
    alongside the HTML document, instead of the typical deferred batch
    that waits on CSS parse. Browser starts downloading during head parse
    rather than after first style recalc.

  Diagnostic surface:
    Small inline script uses the document.fonts API (when available) to
    confirm the preloaded font actually loaded and record the timing.
    Exposed on window.__chaosFontPreload for trace analysis and
    post-deploy verification. No runtime overhead on the font pipeline
    itself; the script runs after the <link> tag has already been parsed
    and the fetch initiated.

  Safety:
    - Missing/rotated hash URL → preload 404 is harmless (browser falls
      back to CSS-discovered loading, same as pre-module behavior)
    - document.fonts API absent → diagnostic degrades to no-op
    - Preload never blocks; no critical path dependency on this module

  Update policy:
    If Shopify rotates the GTStandard hash on a theme update, verify
    via Lighthouse Network waterfall (filter: shop-assets/static_uploads/
    shoplift), update href below.

    If theme CSS changes the @font-face family declaration, update
    User_Font_Family_Primary below to match what document.fonts reports
    (NOT the woff2 filename — those can differ).

  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  v1.3 CHANGELOG (April 24, 2026):
    BUGFIX: v1.2 diagnostic looked for family name "GTStandard-MMedium"
